  "workerNaming": {
    "NOTE": "Each entry is keyed by its Gateway nodeId; uuid/cvmName/composeOut/pinned describe the machine that serves it. The Phala CVM names are crossed against the node ids and that is the live truth: the CVM Phala calls moksha-personal-server-worker-2 serves node moksha-personal-server-worker-1. Verified 2026-09-16 three ways - per-uuid compose read, tee_nodes.compose_hash, and tee_nodes.secret_hash matching each node secret to its node id.",
    "MCP": "Moksha MCP is served by the CONTROLLER (DNS _dstack-app-address.mcp-dev.vana.org resolves to the controller instance), same as mainnet. The mcp-tls service on worker 87c32ca4 is vestigial and not the live endpoint. It is kept this roll so the roll changes no shape; dropping it belongs to a dedicated roll.",
    "instanceIds": "Instance ids come from the Gateway admission record (dp-rpc prd_moksha tee_nodes.instance_id), NOT from phala api /cvms/<uuid>/attestation. That endpoint resolves by APP ID, not uuid, so with two replicas under ec9a39de... the same uuid returns a different quote between calls (measured 2026-09-16: five probes of 1a5acf08 gave eeea1588 x4, 1ac22335 x1). Each admitted node submitted its OWN quote at registration, and tee_nodes.public_url is built from that id - both worker URLs verified answering. FOLLOW-UP: harvest-identity.py must read instance ids from the Gateway admission record, not the Phala API, when replicas share an app id; until it does, render-fleet --stage will refuse at random on this fleet."
  }
